## 2. Recommended Technology Stack

Use a Python-first backend to keep data validation, machine learning, financial calculations, relationship analysis, and evidence processing in one maintainable codebase.

| Component | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| REST API | FastAPI | Backend endpoints |
| Programming language | Python 3.11+ | Business logic and ML |
| API validation | Pydantic v2 | Validated request and response contracts |
| Database | PostgreSQL | Companies, statements, relationships, assessments, and audit records |
| ORM and migrations | SQLAlchemy 2.x, Alembic | Database management |
| Data processing | pandas, NumPy | Financial data processing |
| Baseline ML | scikit-learn | Classification, preprocessing, and evaluation |
| Boosting model | LightGBM or XGBoost | Optional tabular model comparison |
| Model explanations | SHAP | Feature-contribution explanations |
| Graph analysis | NetworkX | Relationship features and graph patterns |
| PDF processing | PyMuPDF and/or pdfplumber | Supported document text and table extraction |
| HTML processing | BeautifulSoup | Parsing permitted public filing pages |
| Tests | pytest | Unit, integration, and leakage tests |
| Deployment | Docker Compose | Repeatable local development |
| Frontend integration | JSON REST API | Dashboard and analyst workflow integration |

Keep the initial implementation modular and avoid unnecessary infrastructure such as Kubernetes, a dedicated feature store, distributed task queues, or a separate graph database.

Document parsing and model training should run as isolated backend jobs when needed, rather than blocking normal dashboard requests.

