## 3. System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    UI[Credit Desk Dashboard] --> API[FastAPI REST API]

    API --> AUTH[Authentication and Authorization]
    AUTH --> SERVICES[Application Services]

    CSV[Financial CSV Imports] --> ING[Data Ingestion and Validation]
    DOC[Financial Documents] --> DOCS[Document Extraction Pipeline]
    REL[Relationship Records] --> GRAPH[Entity Resolution and Graph Engine]
    SRC[Approved Public Sources] --> ING
    SRC --> DOCS
    SRC --> GRAPH

    ING --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
    DOCS --> EVID[Evidence Reconciliation]
    EVID --> DB
    GRAPH --> DB

    DB --> SNAP[Point-in-Time Feature Builder]
    SNAP --> RATIOS[Financial Ratios and Sector Features]
    SNAP --> NET[Relationship Features]
    SNAP --> AUDIT[Verified Document Evidence]

    RATIOS --> DEFAULT[Default Prediction Model]
    RATIOS --> MANIP[Financial Manipulation Screening]
    NET --> MANIP
    AUDIT --> MANIP

    DEFAULT --> RANK[Risk Ranking and 5 Percent Alert Policy]
    MANIP --> RANK

    RANK --> EXPL[SHAP and Evidence-Based Explanation]
    EXPL --> DB

    DB --> API
    API --> UI

    UI --> REVIEW[Analyst Review Actions]
    REVIEW --> DB
    REVIEW --> LOG[Audit Trail]
```

### Architecture rules

1. Every assessment must use data that was publicly available on or before its assessment date.
2. The default prediction model and manipulation screening must remain distinguishable.
3. Relationship signals and document evidence must have their own provenance and verification states.
4. The ranking policy must enforce the review-capacity limit deterministically.
5. Model results, evidence, explanations, and reviewer actions must be traceable.
6. Training must be separated from inference.
7. Failed extraction, missing data, or unavailable predictions must never be treated as a zero-risk result.
8. Demonstration data must be clearly labelled and must not be represented as verified real-world evidence.

