## 15. Hackathon Implementation Order

Build the project in phases. Do not attempt every advanced feature before the core prediction and evaluation pipeline works.

### Phase 1 — Runnable backend

Implement the FastAPI application, PostgreSQL connection, migrations, company records, financial data schemas, health endpoint, validation, and automated tests.

**Acceptance criteria:** The server starts, database migrations work, company records can be created and retrieved, and tests pass.

### Phase 2 — Financial scoring and benchmark model

Audit the UCI data, implement the financial indicators, train baseline models, build the point-in-time feature pipeline, and save versioned model artifacts.

**Acceptance criteria:** Financial calculations are tested, model training is reproducible, and evaluation metrics are produced without leakage claims unsupported by the data.

### Phase 3 — Risk ranking and analyst explanations

Implement the 5% alert policy, cost-aware evaluation, persisted assessments, SHAP where supported, reason codes, and the review workflow.

**Acceptance criteria:** The watch-list is deterministic, never exceeds the configured alert capacity, and exposes traceable explanations.

### Phase 4 — Relationship intelligence

Implement entity and relationship tables, source-based entity resolution, graph features, relationship-path explanations, and verification endpoints.

**Acceptance criteria:** The system can show a sourced relationship path for a test case and distinguishes verified relationships from uncertain matches.

### Phase 5 — Document evidence reconciliation

Implement document metadata, supported PDF/HTML parsing, candidate financial-claim extraction, comparison with structured data, verification states, and mismatch explanations.

**Acceptance criteria:** A test document produces traceable extracted claims and discrepancies; unsupported documents and extraction failures are handled safely.

### Phase 6 — Integrated evaluation and demonstration

Run the UCI benchmark evaluation, prepare the Indian case panel, measure recall at 5%, calculate expected cost, generate supported lead-time curves, and compare baseline versus enhanced configurations.

**Acceptance criteria:** The results are reproducible, the 5% budget is enforced, and the dashboard shows the source and limitations of every material assessment.

